<zk>
	<vlayout spacing="10px" hflex="1">
		<label id="lblTitle" multiline="true">
			ZK-6150 — the popup must dismiss through the framework, not through its own
			document listeners.

			1. Open the calendar, then click this label: the popup closes through the
				framework's own document mousedown (onFloatUp), with no second
				mousedown listener of the component's own.
			2. Open it again and Tab / click into the textbox: focus moving out closes it.
			3. Open it again and press Escape: it closes. It closes even with focus
				outside the box — ownership is canActivate(), not the key's target — so
				a float stacked over the calendar keeps Escape for itself.
		</label>
		<daterangebox id="dr" format="yyyy-MM-dd"/>
		<textbox id="tb"/>

		<label multiline="true">
			4. The plain datebox below shares zul.db.Calendar with the range popup.
				Open it and move the day cursor / switch to the month view: it must
				behave exactly as on a page with no daterangebox on it.
			5. Open the modal window, then open the calendar from the server: Escape
				belongs to the modal, so the calendar stays open.
		</label>
		<datebox id="db" format="yyyy-MM-dd"/>
		<button id="btnModal" label="open modal" onClick="wnd.doModal()"/>
		<window id="wnd" title="modal on top" width="240px" visible="false"
			closable="true">
			<textbox id="wtb"/>
		</window>
	</vlayout>
</zk>
